      "id": "clm_01M4VW9ER9FT7C7HC3GBA84KQB",
      "statement": "The public reading of Neh 8 took place in Nehemiah's governorship (1 Tishri 445), with Ezra and Nehemiah present together.",
      "layer": "reconstruction",
      "passage": "Neh.8.9",
      "classification": "disputed",
      "reasoning": "Keil reads 7:73b–8:2 as the month after the wall's completion and accepts Nehemiah's presence (8:9; 10:1). Batten, following Meyer and Torrey, treats the chapter as Ezra's story placed here by the Chronicler and \"Nehemiah\" in 8:9 as an interpolation. 1 Esdras 9:37–55 (read directly) follows the Ezra 10 account with this reading and names \"Attharates\" instead. The question is tied to the disputed order and dates of Ezra and Nehemiah (see the Ezra 7 decree event).",
